I/IV) degrees of differentiation. Incomplete data are indicated with an asterisk (<sup>&#x0002a;</sup>). Study quality is listed using the results of the Newcastle&#x02013;Ottawa questionnaire (<xref rid="tbl1" ref-type="table">Table 1</xref>). Summary results were either positive (95&#x00025; CI above 1.0) or indeterminate (95&#x00025; CI crossing 1.0). NR=not reported.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>